From e9169771ddc5074ee1e0d87f2fbbfee90fba043b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HaramBlur Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:30:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(experimental): detect & blur CSS background images

First draft toward issue #190 (thumbnails rendered as CSS background
images, e.g. Google Images grid, are currently never checked).

- new module modules/bgImages.js: scans mutated nodes for elements
  with an inline background-image, extracts the url(), sends it
  through the existing imageDetection pipeline, and toggles a
  .hb-bg-blur filter class based on the verdict. A WeakMap avoids
  re-detecting unchanged elements.
- observers.js: one-line hook in the childList mutation handler.
- style.js: keep the bg blur style in sync with blurAmount / gray.

Documented v1 limitations: inline styles only (a getComputedStyle
pass over every mutation would be too expensive), and the filter
blurs the whole element including overlaid text.

NOTE for review: before merging upstream this should be gated behind
a settings toggle (default off) so users can opt into the experiment.
Kept isolated in its own module so it is trivial to revert.
